<title>EGYPT: Egypt raises some cotton export prices till Feb 22.</title>
<headline>Egypt raises some cotton export prices till Feb 22.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Alexandria Cotton Exporters Association (Alcotexa) said on Monday it would raise cotton export prices for three grades and leave other grades unchanged in the 23rd week of the current 96/97 marketing season.</p>
<p>Giza 76, Giza 70 and Giza 77 increased one cent per lb.</p>
<p>The prices, valid until 2200 GMT on February 22, are listed below in centilibres (U.S. cents per lb):</p>
<p>	    FG/EX  FG+1/4  FG    FG-1/4  G/FG  G+3/8</p>
<p>Giza 76  181.0  175.0  169.0  163.0  157.0  154.0 Giza 70  174.0  168.0  162.0  156.0  150.0  147.0 Giza 77  169.0  163.0  157.0  151.0  145.0  142.0 Giza 75  142.0  136.0  130.0  124.0  118.0  115.0 Giza 85  131.0  125.0  119.0  113.0  107.0  104.0 Giza 83  127.0  121.0  115.0  109.0  103.0  100.0 Giza 80  127.0  121.0  115.0  109.0  103.0  100.0 Note - FG/EX = fully good/excellent, G/FG = good/fully good</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
